ckpool is a high-performance, low-overhead Bitcoin solo and pool mining
server written in C. It supports:

- Solo mining (lottery mode) for Bitcoin (BTC)
- Merged mining via AuxPoW (Namecoin, Syscoin, and other SHA-256 chains)
- Stratum protocol for miners
- Multiple auxiliary chains simultaneously
- Very low system resource usage

ckpool is designed to connect directly to a local bitcoind (and optionally
namecoind, syscoind, etc.) via RPC, making it ideal for self-hosted
solo mining setups with small miners such as Bitaxe/NerdAxe devices.
